# ROADMAP: LPC study research code, from now to promotion

**Status:** Draft, proposed by planner (Fable) 2026-10-10 for the human owner's adoption. **Relation to other files:** this file is the plan; `docs/agent/records/work/queue.md` is the live status and stays authoritative for what is open, in progress or done. Where this file and the governance (`docs/agent/governance/`) differ, the governance governs. Unit files under `docs/agent/records/work/` hold each unit's plan, log, review and audit; this file only summarizes them and adds the sub-task breakdown. The test tiers, markers and the blast-radius mechanism named below are defined in `DEVELOPMENT_WORKFLOW.md`.

## 0. How to read this file

- **Identifiers.** WU-0001 to WU-0008 keep their identifiers and are broken into sub-tasks `WU-nnnn.k`. New work starts at WU-0009. Sub-tasks are the unit of planning, implementation and review; a sub-task MAY be executed as its own branch and commit series under the parent unit's file.
- **Owner.** The agent role that executes the task (`planner`, `developer`, `applied-mathematician`, `researcher`, `reviewer`, `critical-elite-auditor`, or `main session` for orchestration), or `human owner` for acts the governance reserves.
- **Class.** CSQ3 development or CSQ2 confirmatory (LPC.PC.5).
- **Serves.** The governance or NVVUQ provision, Methods v2 §M15 item, v3 difference, or defect the task traces to. Nothing here adds study design (LPC.PC.1).
- **Radius.** The blast-radius test set the task needs, in the post-split layout of WU-0010 (`tests/unit/test_<module>.py`, `tests/integration/`, `tests/slow/`, `tests/gpu/`). Until WU-0010 lands, every unit-tier radius means `tests/test_core.py` (14 tests, about 5 s). `smoke` means the smoke preset on CPU on DEV-0 or DEV-3.
- **Effort.** S: under about one hour of agent time. M: up to half a day. L: about a day. No sub-task is planned above M, so the four-hour bound of LPC.PC.10 is checkable per sub-task.
- **Acceptance criteria are fixed now** (VV.3, LPC.AI.6). Where a tolerance says "confirmed by the applied-mathematician", that confirmation happens in the unit's plan before execution and may only tighten the number stated here; it never loosens it after a result is seen (PRIME.2).

## 1. Phases and gates

| Phase | Content | Entry | Exit gate | Owner checkpoint |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| A. Foundations | Repository baseline, environment, test tiers, test-impact tooling, run wrappers, DEF-0007 audit, v3 export and concordance | now | Unit tier green at the gate; WU-0009 to WU-0014 done | Environment set up; v3 exported |
| B. v3 code changes | WU-0001 (seeds, provenance), WU-0002 (Methods v2 §M15 and v3 identifiers), DEV-0 regression against the pilot | A: WU-0009, WU-0010 | Phase-end audit; owner review of seed, provenance, verdict and statistics code queued | Review before the freeze (LPC.PC.11) |
| C. NVVUQ verification | WU-0005 to WU-0008 | B for WU-0006 and WU-0008; A for WU-0005 and WU-0007 | Each gap in `NVVUQ-instantiation-LPC.md` closed or recorded as a known limitation | Review of WU-0006 and WU-0008 before the freeze |
| D. Rehearsal and precision | WU-0003 on the GPU and the CPU: DEV-1 pilot rehearsal, precision report, reproducibility tolerance, DEV-2 full | B, C, WU-0012 | Precision report delivered; tolerance proposed | Sample-size decision; tolerance declared |
| E. Freeze | WU-0004: checklist, pre-freeze audit, owner reviews, full suite, v3 SHA-256, CONF-1 commitment, freeze transaction | D | Freeze ledger entry; tag | The freeze itself |
| F. Confirmatory run and regeneration | WU-0015 confirmatory run; WU-0016 regeneration by another actor (QA.9) | E | Both runs recorded in the manifest; agreement within the declared tolerance | Per-action authorizations (LPC.AUTH.6) |
| G. Reporting and promotion | WU-0017 v3 report and figures; WU-0018 pre-promotion audit and promotion; WU-0019 close-out | F | Promotion ledger entry; retention done | Promotion; governance review (LPC.PC.25) |

**Timeline.** The proposal and methods are due 2026-10-30 and need no results. Phases A and B run in parallel with the writing. The freeze follows the rehearsal (phase D), and the confirmatory run follows the freeze. No calendar dates are fixed for D to G; the compute limits of LPC.AUTH.3 (one run at a time, under 12 h each, 60 GPU-hours per week, development seeds only) bound phase D.

