**Definition of done and acceptance criteria, phase A.**

| Id | Definition of done | Acceptance criteria (checkable) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| WU-0009.1 | `git log` shows one baseline commit of every tracked file; `.gitignore` honored | `git status --porcelain` is empty after the commit; the manifest's "Pilot v1" row gets a dated line naming the baseline commit hash. No file content changes. |
| WU-0009.2 | Environment recorded in the WU-0009 log | `python -c "import jax; print(jax.devices(), jax.config.jax_enable_x64)"` after `import lpcstudy.systems` prints a CUDA device and `True`; `pip freeze` matches every pin in `requirements.txt`; `nvidia-smi` output pasted. `tools/run_tests.sh unit` passes once on CPU. |
| WU-0009.3 | `runs/baseline/smoke/results.json` exists and the manifest cites it | Run on CPU with `JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu` at the baseline commit; `results.json` contains `config.seed == 20261005`; the manifest row records commit, device "cpu", Python and JAX versions. A second CPU run at the same commit is bitwise identical (`cmp` on `results.json` after removing the `seconds` fields): this fixes the CPU-determinism premise of LPC.PC.18 on this machine. If it is not identical, record DEF and stop: the WU-0001 and WU-0002 bitwise criteria then need an owner decision before execution. |
| WU-0009.4 | `queue.md` lists every unit and sub-task in this file | Every WU id in this file appears in `queue.md` with its dependencies; no existing row is edited (append a dated amendment block). |
| WU-0010.1 | Markers registered; conftest in place | `pytest --strict-markers --collect-only -q tests` succeeds; a test placed under `tests/gpu/` carries `gpu`, under `tests/slow/` carries `slow`, and so on (asserted by `tests/unit/test_conftest_markers.py` on a synthetic item); a test outside `tests/gpu/` that calls `jax.devices("gpu")` fails with a clear message when `JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu` is unset. |
| WU-0010.2 | 14 tests pass from their new files; `tests/test_core.py` removed | `pytest -q tests/unit` reports exactly 14 passed; `git diff --stat` shows only moves and import lines (`git diff -M` detects renames). Each file's name matches the module its tests import first. |
| WU-0010.3 | Integration test exists and passes under the `integration` marker | Run under `JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu`; wall-clock under 5 min on the workstation (the smoke preset is about 1 min); the test asserts presence of the four outputs and `validation.gate.gate_pass` is a bool. It is excluded from the `unit` tier by marker. |
| WU-0011.1 | Tool prints a correct test selection for every change class in DEVELOPMENT_WORKFLOW §4.2 | On a synthetic package in `tmp_path` with a known graph: (a) a leaf-module change selects its own test file plus its direct dependents' files; (b) a core-module change selects all transitive dependents plus `tests/integration`; (c) a docs-only or `.claude/`-only change selects nothing and exits 0 with "no tests"; (d) a change in `tests/unit/test_x.py` selects that file only; (e) a change to `requirements.txt`, `pytest.ini` or `tests/conftest.py` selects the whole `unit` tier and prints a warning that this is a gate-sized run; (f) a new module with no test file selects its direct dependents' files and prints a warning; (g) the tool never selects `slow` or `gpu` without `--include-slow` or `--include-gpu`; (h) no pytest process is started without `--run`. Runtime of the selection under 1 s on the real package. |
| WU-0011.2 | Fixture committed; comparison test passes | The fixture is written by reading the `from .x import` statements of each module, including function-level imports; the test asserts the tool's graph equals the fixture exactly. The fixture docstring names it as the independent reference (LPC.PC.21a). A change to the import graph fails this test until the fixture is updated by hand in the same change. |
| WU-0012.1 | Wrapper used by every agent test invocation | Shell test: with the `unit` tier, the child process environment has `JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu`, `OMP_NUM_THREADS`, `MKL_NUM_THREADS` and `OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS` equal to `LPC_THREADS` (default 4), and the pytest arguments include `-q --tb=short -rfE`; with the `gpu` tier, `XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_PREALLOCATE=false` is set and the wrapper exits 75 within 30 s when another process holds the lock. The timeouts are those of DEVELOPMENT_WORKFLOW §4.5. |
| WU-0012.2 | Every `pilot` and `full` run goes through the wrapper | Refuses an id not in `seeds/development_seeds.json`, a raw integer, and any argument containing `confirmatory`, each with exit 64 and a one-line reason. With the lock held, exits 75 at once. Writes `run.meta.json` with `preset`, `seed_id`, `start_utc`, `end_utc`, `device`, `wall_seconds`, `exit_code`. The smoke preset through the wrapper on CPU produces the same `results.json` as a direct invocation. |
| WU-0012.3 | GPU-hour tally available to `dev-run` and the wrapper | On a fixture tree of `run.meta.json` files, the weekly sum matches a hand sum; a start that would exceed 60 h returns exit 65. The wrapper calls it before a `pilot` or `full` start. |
| WU-0013.1 | `docs/agent/records/audits/<date>-def-0007-tests.md` lists all 14 tests with reference, independence and tolerance status | Every test is classified `reference`, `regression guard` or `defective`; each `reference` row names the reference kind from LPC.PC.21a. Tests found self-referential are listed for WU-0013.2. The audit touches no test. |
| WU-0013.2 | Every test has a docstring naming its reference and tolerance justification (`.claude/rules/tests.md`) | All 14 tests pass; `git diff` shows no tolerance that grew (reviewer checks each numeric literal in an `assert` or `approx`); DEF-0007 gets a dated `resolved` line with the audit path. |
| WU-0014.1 | File present with SHA-256 recorded in the WU-0014 log | `sha256sum docs/study/proposal_and_methods_v3.md` recorded; the document states the v3 identifiers of the decision log and experiments E0 to E6. Owner-only: agents have no web access to the Claude Doc. |
| WU-0014.2 | Concordance covers 14 hypothesis rows (H1a–H1d, Q-N, H2a–H2e, gain bound, H3a–H3c), 7 experiments (E0–E6), rules A0–A5, A4o, A* | Every row names the v2 id, the v3 id, the Methods v2 section, and the function in `lpcstudy/analysis.py` or `lpcstudy/experiments.py` that computes it, or "to add in WU-0002.k". The shift experiment appears as "dropped in v3". |
| WU-0014.3 | No open discrepancy without a WU item or a referral | List of discrepancies with their disposition; referrals use the LPC.AI.13 form. |

