**Definition of done and acceptance criteria, phase B.**

| Id | Definition of done | Acceptance criteria (checkable) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| WU-0001.1 | `python -m lpcstudy --preset smoke --seed-id DEV-0` runs; `config.seed_id` and `config.seed` are in `results.json` | Unit: `DEV-0` resolves to 20261005, `DEV-1` to the registry value; `--seed 5` and `--seed-id 5` exit non-zero with a message naming LPC.PC.7; the registry loader rejects a file whose `schema` field differs from `lpcstudy.seed-registry/1`. |
| WU-0001.2 | Commitment check implemented against a ledger file passed as a path | Unit: with a throwaway ledger fixture in `tmp_path` holding a `commitment` entry whose digest the test computes independently with `hashlib.sha256(f"{seed}:{salt}".encode()).hexdigest()`, the check accepts the matching pair and rejects a wrong seed, a wrong salt, and a ledger with no `CONF-1` entry. The real ledger and any real seed never appear in tests (asserted: the fixture path is under `tmp_path`). |
| WU-0001.3 | Every refusal path has a test | Integration: each of the four refusal cases exits with a non-zero code and a one-line reason on stderr, and writes no `results.json`. `--confirmatory` is never invoked outside `tmp_path` fixtures (the `settings.json` deny rule stays). |
| WU-0001.4 | Provenance block present in smoke output and the header label correct | Unit on a fake results dict: every LPC.PC.18 field is present and typed; the confirmatory value never appears in any output (test greps `results.json` and `RESULTS.md` for the fixture seed value); `commit` equals `git rev-parse HEAD` and `dirty` equals `bool(git status --porcelain)`; `peak_rss_bytes` from `resource.getrusage` is greater than 0; `wall_seconds` is within 1% of the elapsed time measured by the test. |
| WU-0001.5 | Numbers unchanged by the unit | On CPU, `--seed-id DEV-0` smoke `results.json` equals `runs/baseline/smoke/results.json` bitwise after removing `provenance`, `seconds` and `handling` keys (the unit adds nothing else); the provenance block parses. |
| WU-0001.6 | `## Review` filled; queue marks "needs owner review before freeze" | Reviewer verdict `approve` or `approve with fixes` with every finding resolved; rounds within DEVELOPMENT_WORKFLOW §2.3. |
| WU-0002.1 | No Lorenz-96, transfer, A4f, τ_d-halved or shift code path remains; smoke runs | `grep -rn "lorenz96\|transfer\|A4f\|shift" lpcstudy/` returns only comments explaining the removal, or nothing; `StudyConfig` has no `transfer_*` fields; `tests/unit` pass; smoke passes the gate on DEV-0. Removed tests are listed in the log with the reason (none of the 14 v1 tests exercises removed code, so none should go). |
| WU-0002.2 | Every hypothesis key in `results.json`, `RESULTS.md` and figure labels is a v3 id | Unit: the identifier table has exactly the rows of the decision-log map (14 rows) and each v2 id maps to the v3 id of that table; `grep -rn "H1f\|H3d" lpcstudy/` finds no live code symbol (v2 `H3d` becomes v3 `H3c`; v2 `H1f` becomes `Q-N`); the docstrings of `config.py` and `data.py` that call the library size ``N``, the `N=` log and result labels in `pipeline.py`, `experiments.py` and `report.py`, and every figure axis for library size read `n_lib`. |
| WU-0002.3 | Exact excess MSE, P3a regime weight and the §M7 K rule implemented with docstrings citing P1(a) and P3(a) | Unit: (a) excess MSE agrees with brute-force minimization of V(w) on a 10⁴-point grid of w in [0, 1], within 10⁻⁶ relative, on 200 random moment triples including cases with u < 0 and u > 1 (the grid spacing of 10⁻⁴ bounds the grid's error by c·(5·10⁻⁵)², which is below 10⁻⁶ relative whenever the test's w is at least 0.1 from w*; the applied-mathematician confirms this before execution); (b) the regime weight agrees with a brute-force minimizer of Σ Vᵢ(w) on the same grid within 10⁻⁶ absolute, on 50 random regimes including all-clipped regimes; (c) the K rule returns the hand-expected K on five fixed excess-vs-K vectors (monotone, flat within 5%, non-monotone, minimum at K = 8, tie at the 5% edge, treated as inside); (d) `test_regret_identity` is kept for the unclipped case and a new test shows the clipped case where c(w − w*)² underestimates V(w) − V(w*) (reference: direct evaluation of the quadratic). |
| WU-0002.4 | H1a uses the median; H1b verdict uses the PLP slope only | Unit: on synthetic per-state ε_s² = b²n^(−2/d) + f² with d = 2.2, multiplied by log-normal noise with 5% of states inflated by a factor of 100 (heavy tail), the median fit recovers 1/d within ±5% at the five `library_sizes` of `StudyConfig` (tolerance from the fit's sensitivity to the median's sampling error at 300 states, confirmed by the applied-mathematician); the H1b result dict has `pass` computed from `slope_plp` only, with `slope_cp` present and ignored (test with CP slope 1.6, PLP slope 1.0 giving pass). |
| WU-0002.5 | Spearman intervals present; N̂ row has no `pass` | Unit: the Spearman point estimate equals `scipy.stats.spearmanr` to 10⁻¹² on 500 bivariate-normal points; the block-bootstrap interval (blocks of 5, 2000 resamples, seed from `make_rng`) contains the point estimate; the `nhat` row has keys `spearman` and `interval` and no `pass`. Coverage is verified in WU-0006. |
| WU-0002.6 | Oracle ΔR² is the primary Q-N output with a reading; deployable is `secondary` | Unit: the reading function returns each of the four readings on intervals constructed to hit each branch, including boundary cases (upper bound exactly 0.05 reads as "≥ 0.05"); the gradient-boosted regressor is constructed with 300 iterations, learning rate 0.05, at most 15 leaves and at least 20 samples per leaf (asserted on the estimator parameters); ΔR² equals R²(four) − R²(three) computed by hand from `sklearn.metrics.r2_score` on a fixed synthetic case to 10⁻¹². |
| WU-0002.7 | H2b(ii) and H2e implemented with curves and intervals | Unit: on a six-state synthetic w* table across the five `library_sizes`, the mean paired change 10³ → 10⁴ equals the hand value to 10⁻¹² and the interval level is 1 − 0.05/3; the mean and median curves have one entry per n_lib with an interval each; H2e on a synthetic error table gives the hand-computed median change, and a state whose CP error is constant across draws yields correlation 0 (not NaN) and increments `handling.zero_variance_corr` by 1. |
| WU-0002.8 | H3a, H3c, H2d match §M11 | Unit: H3a result has `logrank_p_holm` (equal to `holm_adjust` of hand-computed log-rank p's on three synthetic regimes), `iqr_lt`, `pass = all(p < 0.01)` and no regret key; no `H3b` key exists anywhere in results; H3c ratio equals mean(MSE_A5)/mean(MSE_A4) on a synthetic score table to 10⁻¹², with an interval at level 1 − 0.05/3; H2d result has one part and no shift keys. |
| WU-0002.9 | Verdicts follow v3 §7 exactly | Unit: exhaustive enumeration of per-system outcomes {pass, fail, inconclusive}³ (27 cases) gives supported only for (pass, pass, pass), not supported whenever any system fails, inconclusive otherwise; multi-part logic enumerated for two- and three-part criteria (9 and 27 cases); band and bound tests on synthetic intervals including an endpoint exactly on the bound. **Owner decision needed before execution:** Methods v2 §M11 does not state whether an endpoint equal to the bound counts as inside; the planner proposes closed comparison (inside) and the owner records the choice in `decisions.md`. The string "partially supported" appears nowhere in `lpcstudy/`. |
| WU-0002.10 | Gate has V7; full preset sweep states 1000 | Unit: `gate_status` returns `V7` and `gate_pass` requires it; V7 passes on a synthetic cell with δ/(ρν) = 1 and fails at 0.85; `FULL.n_test_sweep == 1000`, `PILOT.n_test_sweep == 300`; smoke output lists V1–V7. |
| WU-0002.11 | Every DEF-0001 case counted and reported; nothing silent | Unit: injecting one non-finite estimate increments `handling.invariant_mean_replacements` by 1; one error of 20 σ_x increments `handling.error_clips`; a regime map with an empty leaf increments `handling.regime_count_fallback`; each nonzero counter writes one `run.log` line. Smoke `results.json` has the `handling` block for every cell with every counter present (zero allowed). Reviewer greps for `np.clip`, `nan_to_num`, `np.where(np.isfinite` and confirms each site is counted. |
| WU-0002.12 | Comparison table in the WU-0002 log and in `docs/study/dev_regression_dev0.md` labeled `DEVELOPMENT (DEV-0): not a hypothesis test` | Every quantity recorded in `pilot_results_v1.json` that the unit does not intend to change agrees bitwise, or within 10⁻¹² relative where a summation order changed: the `context` block (λ_max, τ_d, τ_ac, spacing, obs_scale), the `validation` numbers V1–V6, the fitted proxy coefficients, the rule `scores`, and the unchanged hypothesis statistics. (The pilot JSON holds summaries only, not per-state oracle moments or w*; those are compared only through the summaries they feed.) Every changed statistic is listed with old and new value and the §M15 item that changed it. **Risk R1 applies:** the pilot was produced on different hardware and is not under version control; if the `context` floats differ beyond 10⁻¹² relative, the run is not bitwise reproducible here for reasons unrelated to the code. The fallback criterion, to be fixed by the owner before this run, is: integer context quantities (τ_d, τ_ac, spacing) identical; λ_max within the Benettin sampling error stated by the applied-mathematician; each unchanged pilot statistic inside the pilot's own 95% interval where one exists; the V1–V6 checks passing at their §M10 criteria. The run is CPU-only (bitwise identity is expected on CPU only, LPC.PC.18) and goes through `tools/run_preset.sh` with `LPC_THREADS=8`. |
| WU-0002.13 | `## Review` per sub-task; owner checkpoint queued | As WU-0001.6. Verdict and statistics code (WU-0002.3 to .9) is marked "needs owner review before freeze". |

