**Definition of done and acceptance criteria, phase C.**

| Id | Definition of done | Acceptance criteria (checkable) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| WU-0005.1 | Test in `test_systems` passes | Reference: `scipy.linalg.expm(A t) x0` for a fixed 3×3 A with complex eigenvalues (independent of the integrator). Steps h, h/2, h/4 chosen so that the finest error is above 10⁻¹¹ (well above round-off) and the coarsest below 10⁻³; observed order in [3.8, 4.2]. Uses `make_flow_step` on a `SystemSpec` built in the test with the linear field and `max_dt` set to each step. Under 5 s. |
| WU-0005.2 | Test in `test_ensemble` passes | 10⁴ library vectors in ℝ⁷ and 200 queries from `np.random.default_rng(<fixed>)`: nearest index identical to an exhaustive `np.argmin` of squared distances for every query (exact), nearest distance within 10⁻¹² relative (round-off of a 7-term sum). Second-nearest also checked where the margin is reported. |
| WU-0005.3 | Test in `test_oracle` passes | Sets: uniform on a line segment, a unit square and a unit cube embedded in ℝ⁷ by a fixed orthonormal map, 2×10⁴ points, k = 20 (the study's setting). Estimate within ±10% of 1, 2 and 3 respectively; the applied-mathematician confirms this from the estimator's bias and variance at k = 20 and n = 2×10⁴ before execution, and may tighten it. Fixed seed. |
| WU-0005.4 | Residual and iteration count per estimate in the cell results and summarized in `results.json` (`median_residual`, `p95_residual`, `median_iterations`, `fraction_no_decrease`) | Unit: starting from the true state with no noise and the exact model, every accepted step keeps the cost non-increasing (asserted per iteration) and the final residual is at most 10⁻¹²·D (float64 round-off on D = 7 squared terms); the iteration count reported equals the number of accepted steps counted by the test. Smoke output shows the summary per cell. |
| WU-0005.5 | Per-state check implemented and reported for the core cell of each system in the rehearsal | The applied-mathematician fixes the exact empirical form of P2(c) before execution (which quantity plays Ȳ, and whether the expectation is taken over the same M draws). Unit: on a synthetic library with a chosen margin Δ and noise ρ, the bound holds for every state (fraction of violations 0), and a case with ‖η‖ < Δ/2 for all draws gives N = 0. Slow: on a development cell, the fraction of states violating the bound is reported in `results.json` and is 0 when the bound is evaluated on the same draws; any nonzero fraction is a defect, not a tolerance. |
| WU-0005.6 | `## Review` filled; note with proposed status lines | Each of the five instantiation rows gets a proposed `met` line with the test name as evidence. |
| WU-0006.1 | Harness reusable by .2 and .3 | Each test states R and the Monte Carlo standard error `sqrt(p(1 − p)/R)` for a coverage p in its docstring; data generation uses `make_rng(seed, "wu0006", <name>)`; runtime of the whole `tests/slow/` directory under 30 min on CPU with `LPC_THREADS=4`. |
| WU-0006.2 | Coverage results recorded in the unit file and the tests pass | R = 1000 replications per statistic, level and dependence setting. Acceptance: empirical coverage ≥ nominal − 3·sqrt(nominal(1 − nominal)/R), that is ≥ 0.929 at 95% and ≥ 0.971 at 98.3%. Undercoverage below that bound fails the test and opens a DEF; it is never tuned away. Truth values: the population quantity of the generating process (for the median and Spearman, computed analytically or from 10⁷ draws, stated in the test). The paired change and MSE ratio use paired AR(1) series with a known mean difference and ratio. |
| WU-0006.3 | Size and null-coverage tests pass | Log-rank with Holm: three regimes with equal geometric hazards, 200 states each, R = 2000 families: family-wise rejection rate at the 0.01 level ≤ 0.01 + 3·sqrt(0.01·0.99/2000) = 0.0167. Null ΔR²: target independent of the fourth coordinate given the other three (synthetic, 3000 training and 1000 test states, R = 500): N2, the lower bound exceeds 0 in at most 22 of 500 replications; N3, the 95% interval contains the conditional gain of the two fitted models (training held fixed) in at least 461 of 500; N1, the interval contains 0, is reported (it fails by construction, DEF-0021). Under Option C (DEC-0026 item 2) N1 to N3 and the other nominal bounds are recorded, not asserted; the pre-registered consistency ranges are asserted. |
| WU-0006.4 | Reviews recorded | The applied-mathematician's section confirms each Monte Carlo error statement; the reviewer confirms no R, level or bound changed after a result was seen (compares the plan's numbers with the tests'). Marked "needs owner review before freeze". |
| WU-0007.1 | `docs/agent/notes/<date>-research-lyapunov.md` with one row per system | Each row: value, source with DOI or URL, status `confirmed`, quote, integrator and step conditions, date. Values from memory are labeled `unconfirmed (memory)` and not used. At most 50 pages for the unit (LPC.AUTH.2). |
| WU-0007.2 | Test passes or a DEF records the discrepancy | The code's `estimate_lyapunov` at the configured interval agrees with the confirmed value within 3% relative (Benettin estimates over 2×10⁵ steps carry a standard error near 1%; the applied-mathematician confirms or tightens before execution). A larger discrepancy is reported with the step size as the suspected cause (LPC.NV.1) and is not tuned away. The Methods v2 §M2 values (0.905, 0.0719, 0.431) are compared with the confirmed values in the note. |
| WU-0007.3 | `RESULTS.md` validation section has the three comparisons and the sentence that validation against a real-world referent does not apply (NVVUQ.13) | `test_report` asserts both on a fake results dict. |
| WU-0008.1 | Budget tables generated from `results.json` by `--report-only` | For each of the five primary QoIs, a table with the eight rows of the `uq-budget` skill; every row shows a size or "not estimated: <reason>"; `test_report` checks the row set and that no cell is empty. |
| WU-0008.2 | Numerical rows have numbers | Bootstrap endpoint Monte Carlo error: for the percentile q at B = 2000 resamples, the binomial standard error of the percentile index `sqrt(q(1 − q)/B)` converted to the statistic's scale by the empirical bootstrap distribution; checked against a nested bootstrap on one fixed synthetic case within a factor of 2 (the nested bootstrap's own error; the applied-mathematician confirms). Oracle Monte Carlo row from the V4 half-width at M = 200. LM row from WU-0005.4. V6 row from the validation results. Each numerical row flags `below 10% of the sampling half-width: yes/no`. |
| WU-0008.3 | Every interval-bearing figure and table carries its label | `test_report` greps the generated `RESULTS.md` for the four label elements next to every interval table; figure captions include the level and "moving-block bootstrap, blocks of 5". |
| WU-0008.4 | Table present with one row per QoI of the identifier table | `test_report` asserts row count equals the identifier table's tested rows plus Q-N. |
| WU-0008.5 | Reviews recorded | Marked "needs owner review before freeze". |

