**Definition of done and acceptance criteria, phase E.** WU-0004.1: every checklist item of the `freeze-checklist` skill is marked done with evidence, or the owner waives it by ledger entry. WU-0004.2: all tiers pass once; the `slow` tier runs once and its coverage numbers are pasted; no test is rerun. WU-0004.4: the audit file lists zero open blockers. WU-0004.5: the owner's review is recorded in each unit's `## Review` under their name. WU-0004.6: `tools/ledger.py verify` passes and the entry has `seed_id: CONF-1` and a 64-hex digest; the owner confirms the seed and salt are stored outside the repository; an agent later checks that no log, unit file or output echoes an `LPC_CONF_SEED` or `LPC_CONF_SALT` value. WU-0004.7: `python3 tools/ledger.py status` shows every governed file adopted and unchanged; the tag points at the committed hash in the entry.

### Phase F. Confirmatory run and regeneration (owner-authorized)

| Id | Title | Owner | Depends on | Class | Serves | Radius | Effort |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| WU-0015.1 | Pre-run checks: working tree clean at `freeze-1`, environment matches `requirements.lock`, no other preset run on the CPU, `LPC_THREADS=8` as frozen, the run lock free, per-action authorization recorded (LPC.AUTH.6) | human owner (authorization), main session (checks) | WU-0004.7 | CSQ2 | LPC.AUTH.6, LPC.PC.7 | none | S |
| WU-0015.2 | Confirmatory run (official): full preset, `--confirmatory`, seed and salt supplied by the owner at run time through the environment, on the CPU with `LPC_THREADS=8` through `tools/run_preset.sh`, under the lock | human owner (or an agent under the per-action authorization) | WU-0015.1 | CSQ2 | LPC.PC.7, LPC.PC.8, NVVUQ.18 | none | M (wall-clock) |
