| WU-0016.4 | Manifest entry for run-2; comparison report committed | human owner | WU-0016.3 | CSQ2 | LPC.PC.15 | none | S |

**Definition of done and acceptance criteria, phase F.** WU-0015.1: `git status --porcelain` empty and `git describe --tags` equals `freeze-1`; `pip freeze` equals `requirements.lock`; the ledger holds the per-action `authorization` entry quoting the owner's words. WU-0015.2: the code's commitment check passes (the run refuses otherwise); the header reads `CONFIRMATORY: UNPROMOTED`; the seed value appears in no output (the provenance block carries only `CONF-1`); wall-clock under 12 h; provenance records the CPU device and `LPC_THREADS=8`. WU-0015.2b: the comparison report is committed; a differing verdict-type leaf, a failing TD part or a GPU gate failure is recorded as information and changes no verdict. WU-0016.3: the tool reports, per QoI, the absolute and relative difference and whether it is within tolerance; unit test on two synthetic results files with one planted out-of-tolerance value fails that QoI only. WU-0016.2 and .4: tier T0 (bitwise) on the same platform; otherwise every QoI within the WU-0003.6 tolerance of its tier and every verdict identical; otherwise a DEF is opened and promotion is blocked (LPC.PC.14).

