**Definition of done and acceptance criteria, phase G.** WU-0017.1: `--report-only` on the confirmatory `results.json` regenerates `RESULTS.md` identically on two runs; every number in the narrative is traceable to a key in `results.json` (the auditor samples ten); every reported QoI carries the six NVVUQ.22 items; every interval carries the four NVVUQ.16 items; the three primaries are labeled with level 1 − 0.05/3 and the intersection–union rule is stated. WU-0017.2: every figure caption names its experiment, its v3 identifier and the interval procedure; `grep` of the figure code and captions finds no shift, transfer, Lorenz-96 or A4f reference. WU-0018.1: audit file with zero blockers. WU-0018.3: `tools/ledger.py verify` passes; the manifest row names the `promotion` entry.

## 3. Dependency and critical-path view

The critical path, in order. Everything not listed runs in parallel off the path.

| Step | Task | Why it is on the path |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | WU-0009.1, WU-0009.2 | Nothing can be committed or run on the GPU before the baseline commit and the environment exist |
| 2 | WU-0010.1, WU-0010.2 | The tiers and the module-per-file split are what the blast-radius rule and every later radius refer to |
| 3 | WU-0009.3 | The smoke reference that WU-0001.5 compares against must come from the baseline commit, before any code change |
| 4 | WU-0001.1 to .5 | Seed ids and provenance are prerequisites for every later development run to be recorded under REPRO |
| 5 | WU-0002.1 to .11 | The v3 code changes; WU-0002.3 (excess MSE, regime weight, K rule) and WU-0002.9 (verdicts) are the longest sub-tasks and gate WU-0006 and WU-0008 |
| 6 | WU-0002.12 | The DEV-0 regression is the first long CPU run and must precede the rehearsal, because it validates the unchanged quantities |
| 7 | WU-0006.1 to .3 | Statistical verification is required before confirmatory use at CSQ2 (NVVUQ.23) and depends on the final form of the statistics |
| 8 | WU-0003.2 to .4 | The rehearsal and the reproducibility tolerance are freeze prerequisites (LPC.PC.6) |
| 9 | WU-0003.6 | The owner's sample-size and tolerance decisions |
| 10 | WU-0004.1 to .8 | The freeze |
| 11 | WU-0015, WU-0016 | Confirmatory run, then regeneration by another actor |
| 12 | WU-0017, WU-0018 | Report, pre-promotion audit, promotion |

**Off the critical path, with their latest start.** WU-0011 and WU-0012 (tooling): before the first `pilot` run (WU-0002.12). WU-0013 (DEF-0007): before the freeze checklist. WU-0014 (v3 export and concordance): the concordance must close before WU-0002.13's owner review, since it is the check that the code implements v3 and not only the stated differences. WU-0005 and WU-0007: any time after WU-0010; they feed WU-0008.2 and the freeze checklist. WU-0008.1 to .4: after WU-0002.9 and WU-0005.4, before WU-0003.2 so the rehearsal report carries budget tables.

**Parallel lanes for several agents.** Lane 1: WU-0001 then WU-0002.1–.3. Lane 2: WU-0010 then WU-0011 then WU-0012. Lane 3: WU-0005 and WU-0007 (researcher dispatch), then WU-0013. WU-0002.4–.11 split across lanes once WU-0002.2 has merged, since they touch disjoint functions of `analysis.py`; merge conflicts in `analysis.py` and `report.py` are expected and resolved by the main session, never by history rewrite. Each lane is a git worktree (DEVELOPMENT_WORKFLOW §3).

