| When | What the owner does | Provision |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Phase A start | Adopts the governance (ledger entries), fills LPC.PC.23 and LPC.AUTH.4, sets up the environment (WU-0009.2), exports v3 (WU-0014.1) | GOV.41, LPC.AUTH.1 |
| Before WU-0002.9 executes | Decides the boundary convention for interval endpoints on a bound | VV.3, REPRO.7 |
| Before WU-0002.12 executes | Decides the fallback regression criterion if the pilot is not bitwise reproducible on the workstation (risk R1) | VV.3 |
| Phase B end | Reviews seed and provenance code (WU-0001) and verdict and statistics code (WU-0002.3–.9) | LPC.PC.11 |
| Phase C end | Reviews WU-0006 and WU-0008 | LPC.PC.11 |
| Phase D | Authorizes the optional DEV-2 full run; records the sample-size decision and the reproducibility tolerance | LPC.AUTH.3, LPC.PC.18 |
| Phase E | Every WU-0004 item from .4 onward | LPC.PC.8 |
| Phase F | Per-action authorizations for the confirmatory run and the regeneration; releases outputs | LPC.AUTH.6, LPC.PC.13 |
| Phase G | Promotion; retention; governance review | LPC.PC.13, LPC.PC.19, LPC.PC.25 |
| Any time | Rulings on referrals; waivers; stopping-rule extensions | PRIME.14, LPC.PC.10 |

## 5. Out of scope

Refused or spun off under LPC.PC.1 and LPC.AI.11; an agent that finds one necessary records a note and refers:

- Lorenz-96 and transfer experiments (dropped by D3; WU-0002.1 removes the code);
- a misspecified-model forecaster arm (future work, Methods v2 §M16; the ±5% and ±10% perturbation stays as the E6 robustness variant);
- Lean formalization of P1–P3;
- new hypotheses, systems, rules or criteria not in the v3 design, including a corrected N̂ (DEF-0008) and the doubled-thinning check (DEF-0009), which are reported as limitations;
- performance optimization not driven by a measured shortfall against the 12-hour full-preset budget (LPC.PC.22, RSRC.4);
- new dependencies, including `pytest-xdist` and `pytest-timeout`, unless recorded as a decision under LPC.PC.17 (the wrappers use thread caps and coreutils `timeout` instead);
- changes to governance or `.claude/` by agents (proposals only).

## 6. Risks and open items

| Id | Risk | Mitigation in this plan |
| --- | --- | --- |
| R1 | The pilot was produced in a sandbox on different hardware and is not under version control (manifest). Bitwise reproduction on the workstation is not assured; chaotic trajectories amplify any one-ulp difference, so a mismatch at step one invalidates the bitwise criterion of WU-0002.12 for reasons unrelated to the code. | WU-0009.3 establishes CPU-to-CPU determinism on the workstation first; the owner fixes the fallback criterion before WU-0002.12 runs. |
| R2 | The v3 document is not in the bundle; the code changes rely on the stated differences. | WU-0014 exports it and builds the concordance before the owner review of WU-0002. |
| R3 | The `slow` tier (WU-0006) could grow past the 30-minute budget. | Budget is an acceptance criterion of WU-0006.1; R is fixed per test and not increased without a plan amendment. |
| R4 | Parallel agents contend for the GPU or oversubscribe the CPU. | WU-0012 wrappers; DEVELOPMENT_WORKFLOW §4.5. |
| R5 | The weekly 60 GPU-hour cap is reached by the rehearsal plus the optional full run. | WU-0012.3 tally; the full run on DEV-2 is optional and owner-authorized. |
| R6 | Repository is not yet a git repository; CLAUDE.md commands and skills assume one. | WU-0009.1 is the first task. |

